Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tests: generated shape corpus for nested-heredoc
 masking (card comment 10718 item 2)

A seeded sample (2400 of 17320 cases) of the product of shell option words
(-s before, after, bundled or absent; allowlisted words plus -i/-l/--login,
-o history/histexpand, -H, -k, -O, --rcfile/--init-file, -, ...) x stdin
wrappers (env, timeout, nice, nohup, command, stdbuf) x nesting forms (plain,
function, subshell, ssh, outer bash -s) x payloads (startup-file rewrite,
history expansion, wrapped inner consumer, inner function) x bash/sh. Real
bash runs every case with a fake hermes; a $HOME whose .bash_profile/.bashrc
rewrite stdin and whose .profile/ENV put a python3-that-is-bash on PATH.
Property: if bash ran the walk-only payload and origin/main refuses the
command (checked-in verdicts, main da52aff8f4), this tree refuses it too.
The six rows of review 5887281618 are labelled rows of the corpus.

Violations (sample 2400 / full 17320): ab4ef60746 51 / 343; c3ee55588d 0 / 0
(this commit changes tests only, so the guard is byte-identical to c3ee55588d).

Also the live 23:13 PT MacBook shape (scp && timeout ssh host 'bash -l -s'
<<'EOS' | grep, nested python3 body reading ~/.hermes/kanban.db): refused on
main, allowed here because the path is only a call argument (a mention).
